<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>When you're pricing barbed wire fence installation in Waco, TX, the numbers that matter are per foot and per mile. A 5-strand barbed wire fence from Brazos Ridge Fence Co. runs $2.50 to $5.50 per linear foot installed, depending on terrain, post type, and how much old fence we're tearing out first. Net wire and field fence for goats, sheep, and horses runs $3.50 to $8 per foot. Those are real installed prices, not teaser rates that grow once we're on your place.</p><p>We build fence across McLennan, Bosque, and Falls counties, from small hobby tracts near <a href="/fence-builder-lorena/">Lorena</a> to full ranch perimeters out past <a href="/fence-builder-crawford/">Crawford</a>. Every job starts with a free written estimate, and we're licensed and insured. If you're comparing options, our <a href="/ranch-fence-cost/">ranch fence cost guide</a> breaks down every fence type we build.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">5-Strand Barbed Wire</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">The workhorse of Central Texas cattle fencing at $2.50 to $5.50 per linear foot installed. Tight strands, proper spacing, and corners braced to hold tension for decades.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Net Wire and Field Fence</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">For goats, sheep, horses, and mixed stock, net wire runs $3.50 to $8 per foot installed. It stops the escape artists that walk right through barbed wire.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">T-Post or Pipe-Post Builds</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">We'll tell you straight where T-posts do the job and where pipe earns its cost. Most perimeters use steel T-posts on line with pipe at corners, gates, and braces.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Ag-Exemption Perimeters</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A stock-tight perimeter fence is the backbone of a grazing operation, and grazing use is what county appraisal districts look for. We build fence that actually holds cattle.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">24/7 Storm-Damage Repair</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Tree through the fence at 2 a.m. and cattle headed for the highway? Our emergency line answers around the clock and we'll get wire back up fast.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#2A2724;margin:0 0 8px;">Free Written Estimates</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">We walk your fence line, measure it, and hand you a written price per foot. No pressure, no vague ranges, no surprises on the invoice.</p>
      </div>
</div>
